{"name":"Indochine","hex":"#9c5b34","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Mainland Southeast Asia","blocks":[{"text":"Mainland Southeast Asia is the continental portion of Southeast Asia. It comprises the countries of Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar, Peninsular Malaysia, Singapore, Thailand, and Vietnam. MSEA borders East Asia to the north, South Asia to the west, and Maritime Southeast Asia to the south and east."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Mainland_Southeast_Asia_%28orthographic_projection%29.svg/330px-Mainland_Southeast_Asia_%28orthographic_projection%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mainland_Southeast_Asia","wikidata":"Q43467"},{"title":"French Indochina","blocks":[{"text":"French Indochina, officially known as the Indochinese Union and after 1941 as the Indochinese Federation, was a group of French-dependent territories in Southeast Asia from 1887 to 1954. It was initially a federation of French colonies (1887–1949), later a confederation of French associated states (1949–1954). It comprised Cambodia, Laos, Guangzhouwan (1898–1945), Cochinchina, and Vietnamese regions of Tonkin and Annam. It was established in 1887 and was dissolved in 1954. In 1949, Vietnam was reunited and it regained Cochinchina. Its capitals were Hanoi (1902–1945) and Saigon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c3/Flag_of_France.svg/330px-Flag_of_France.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Indochina","wikidata":"Q185682"},{"title":"Indochine (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Indochine is a 1992 French period drama film set in colonial French Indochina from the 1930s to the 1950s. It is the story of Éliane Devries, a French plantation owner, and of her adopted Vietnamese daughter, Camille, set against the backdrop of the rising Vietnamese nationalist movement. The screenplay was written by novelist Érik Orsenna, screenwriters Louis Gardel and Catherine Cohen, and director Régis Wargnier. The film stars Catherine Deneuve, Vincent Pérez, Linh Dan Pham, Jean Yanne and Dominique Blanc. The film won the Academy Award for Best Foreign Language Film at the 65th Academy Awards, and Deneuve was nominated for Best Actress."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/29/Indochine-movie-poster-1992-french.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indochine_(film)","wikidata":"Q1130644"},{"title":"Indochine (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Indochine is a French rock and new wave band formed in Paris in 1981. It achieved significant success in the 1980s across the Francophone world, Europe, and Latin America with hit songs L'Aventurier and Canary Bay. After releasing several critically praised but commercially disappointing albums in the 1990s, the band experienced a resurgence with the 2002 album Paradize. To date, Indochine has sold over 10 million albums and singles worldwide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/2013-03-23_Concert_Indochine_-_Brest_%285%29.JPG/330px-2013-03-23_Concert_Indochine_-_Brest_%285%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indochine_(band)","wikidata":"Q1122583"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Mekong_River_in_Laos_%281490866472%29.jpg/500px-Mekong_River_in_Laos_%281490866472%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Mekong_River_in_Laos_%281490866472%29.jpg/1280px-Mekong_River_in_Laos_%281490866472%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Mekong_River_in_Laos_%281